  "question": {
    "text": "An ellipse passes through the foci of the hyperbola, <math><mn>9</mn><msup><mrow><mi>x</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup><mo>-</mo><mn>4</mn><msup><mrow><mi>y</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup><mo>=</mo><mn>36</mn></math> and its major and minor axes lie along the transverse and conjugate axes of the hyperbola respectively. If the product of eccentricities of the two conics is <math><mfrac><mrow><mn>1</mn></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></mfrac><mo>,</mo></math> then which of the following points does not lie on the ellipse?",
    "image": null
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "id": "1wNEk",
      "text": "<math><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mfrac><mrow><msqrt><mn>39</mn></msqrt></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></mfrac><mo>,</mo><mi> </mi><msqrt><mn>3</mn></msqrt></mrow></mfenced></math>",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    },
    {
      "id": "u661J",
      "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mfrac><msqrt><mn>13</mn></msqrt><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mo>,</mo><mi>&#160;</mi><mfrac><msqrt><mn>3</mn></msqrt><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mrow></mfenced></math>",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": true
    },
    {
      "id": "9ZrfC",
      "text": "<math><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><msqrt><mfrac><mrow><mn>13</mn></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></mfrac></msqrt><mo>,</mo><mi> </mi><msqrt><mn>6</mn></msqrt></mrow></mfenced></math>",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    },
    {
      "id": "KmTOV",
      "text": "<math><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><msqrt><mn>13</mn></msqrt><mo>,</mo><mi> </mi><mn>0</mn></mrow></mfenced></math>",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    }
  ],
  "correctValue": null,
  "solution": {
    "text": "<p>Equation of the hyperbola<br /><math><mfrac><mrow><msup><mrow><mi>x</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup></mrow><mrow><mn>4</mn></mrow></mfrac><mo>-</mo><mfrac><mrow><msup><mrow><mi>y</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup></mrow><mrow><mn>9</mn></mrow></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></math><br /><br /><img src=\"https://cdn-question-pool.getmarks.app/pyq/jee_main/127ae8da-47e1-4ef0-818c-cc3c01564de4-image.png\" style=\"width: 300px; height: 192px;\" /><br /><br />Focus of hyperbola <math><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><msub><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">a</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><msub><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">e</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&nbsp;</mi><mn>0</mn></mrow></mfenced></math> and <math><mo>(</mo><mo>-</mo><msub><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">a</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><msub><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">e</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&nbsp;</mi><mn>0</mn><mo>)</mo></math>&nbsp;&nbsp;<br /><br /><math><msub><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">a</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&nbsp;</mi><msub><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">e</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&nbsp;</mi><msqrt><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>9</mn></mrow><mrow><mn>4</mn></mrow></mfrac></msqrt><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><msqrt><mn>13</mn></msqrt></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></mfrac></math><br /><br /><math><mo>&there4;</mo></math> Foci would be <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mo>+</mo><msqrt><mn>13</mn></msqrt><mo>,</mo><mi>&nbsp;</mi><mn>0</mn></mrow></mfenced></math> and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mo>-</mo><msqrt><mn>13</mn></msqrt><mo>,</mo><mi>&nbsp;</mi><mn>0</mn></mrow></mfenced></math>&nbsp;<br /><br />Product of eccentricity would be&nbsp;<br /><br /><math><mfrac><mrow><msqrt><mn>13</mn></msqrt></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></mfrac><mi>&nbsp;</mi><mo>&sdot;</mo><msub><mrow><mi>e</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>1</mn></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></mfrac></math><br /><br /><math><mo>&there4;</mo><mi>&nbsp;</mi><mi>&nbsp;</mi><msub><mrow><mi>e</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><mi>&nbsp;</mi><mfrac><mrow><mn>1</mn></mrow><mrow><msqrt><mn>13</mn></msqrt></mrow></mfrac></math> .<br /><br />As the major &amp; minor axis of the ellipse coincide with axis of hyperbola then the value of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>a</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></math>&nbsp;for ellipse would be <math><msqrt><mn>13</mn></msqrt></math> ,<br /><br /><math><msub><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">e</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><msqrt><mn>1</mn><mo>-</mo><mfrac><mrow><msubsup><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">b</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></msubsup></mrow><mrow><msubsup><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">a</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></msubsup></mrow></mfrac></msqrt></math><br /><br /><math><mfrac><mrow><mn>1</mn></mrow><mrow><msqrt><mn>13</mn></msqrt></mrow></mfrac><mo>=</mo><msqrt><mn>1</mn><mo>-</mo><mfrac><mrow><msubsup><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">b</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></msubsup></mrow><mrow><mn>13</mn></mrow></mfrac></msqrt></math><br /><br /><math><msubsup><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">b</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></msubsup><mo>=</mo><mn>12</mn></math><br /><br /><math><mo>&there4;</mo></math> Equation of the ellipse would be&nbsp;<br /><br /><math><mfrac><mrow><msup><mrow><mi>x</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup></mrow><mrow><mn>13</mn></mrow></mfrac><mo>+</mo><mfrac><mrow><msup><mrow><mi>y</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup></mrow><mrow><mn>12</mn></mrow></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>.</mo></math><br /><br />Option (1)&nbsp;&nbsp;<math><mfrac><mrow><mn>39</mn></mrow><mrow><mn>4</mn><mi>&nbsp;</mi><mo>&sdot;</mo><mo>(</mo><mn>13</mn><mo>)</mo></mrow></mfrac><mo>+</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>3</mn></mrow><mrow><mn>12</mn></mrow></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></math><br /><br />Satisfies the equation, hence it lies on the ellipse.&nbsp;<br /><br />Option (2)&nbsp;<math><mfrac><mrow><mn>13</mn></mrow><mrow><mn>4</mn><mi>&nbsp;</mi><mo>(</mo><mn>13</mn><mo>)</mo></mrow></mfrac><mo>+</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>3</mn></mrow><mrow><mn>4.12</mn></mrow></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></math><br /><br />does not lie on the ellipse.<br /><br />Option (3)&nbsp;&nbsp;<math><mfrac><mrow><mn>13</mn></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo>(</mo><mn>13</mn><mo>)</mo></mrow></mfrac><mo>+</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>6</mn></mrow><mrow><mn>12</mn></mrow></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></math> satisfy.<br /><br />Option (4) <math><mfrac><mrow><mn>13</mn></mrow><mrow><mn>13</mn></mrow></mfrac><mo>+</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></math> satisfy.<br /><br />So, option <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mfrac><msqrt><mn>13</mn></msqrt><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mo>,</mo><mi>&nbsp;</mi><mfrac><msqrt><mn>3</mn></msqrt><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mrow></mfenced></math> is the answer.</p>",
